From 5f1a101d79c45d506f93a103bc974329647c30e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:32:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] fix(SPA-PUNCH-01): draw a punched hole as the mark the
 child places
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The hole on the folded stack was a fixed 22px disc with a 4px cream
border and a 3px dark ring — dark fill, light ring, dark ring. It read
as an eye, resembled neither a hole nor anything else on screen, and at
36px overall it outgrew its grid square and straddled the paper's edge,
so a hole that was arithmetically in the right cell looked misplaced.

It is now the same object the child places on the answer sheet: a filled
navy square with a cream dot, matching .mcell.on. Size comes from --cell
so it fills exactly one square at every grid size (4, 6 and 8) instead
of a fixed width that only suited the coarsest. The sequence-strip chip
moves to the same cream so all three depictions of a hole agree.

Verified through the review UI's own host path (init + start into an
iframe), not just a standalone load.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 apps/web/public/exam-demos/SPA-PUNCH-01.html        | 13 +++++++++++--
 .../exam-question-types/demos/SPA-PUNCH-01.html     | 13 +++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

