Every flap swept through negative local Z, so it rotated behind the
sheet and the sheet hid it. The child saw the paper abruptly halve with
no visible fold — which is the one thing this item needs them to watch,
since the whole task is tracking where a hole lands through the layers.
All four cases carried the same sign error, so all four are negated:
vertical, horizontal, and both diagonals now sweep in front.

Timing is 25% slower (340ms to 425ms per fold, 80ms to 100ms between)
so a three- or four-fold sequence stays followable. Both values are now
named constants rather than literals buried in the loop.

Verified frame by frame through the host path on all three axes.

