From b31e229b7bfd731ba577cbf33c50bcfc111eff95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:23:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(SPA-PICKFOLD-01): punch where the item says, not in
 the middle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The preview drew one hole at the centre of whatever rectangle was left
after folding and never read content.punches at all. Every item in the
bank punches a corner, and a centre punch unfolds to a different pattern
than the one the child is asked to match — so the animation contradicted
the question it was illustrating.

Holes are now drawn at the cells the item names, measured from the
folded stack's own corner, which is the space those coordinates are in:
folding L then T then B on item 2 leaves columns 4-7 and rows 4-5, and a
corner punch there unfolds to x in {3,4}, y in {0,3,4,7} — exactly its
recorded target.

Items with two punches drew one hole; both are drawn now, each wearing
the mark its holes wear in the target pattern (coral circle for the
first, violet diamond for the second) so the child can tell which punch
produced which marks.

A punch can fall outside the stack while previewing a WRONG fold order,
which leaves a smaller stack than the item was built for; that is
clamped so the preview stays on the paper.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
