From b36f54eda1daf1091aa9b7d5817de9078a088d8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aadi Takle <aadiatakle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:25:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(SPA-PUNCH-01): let the sheet open before the first
 crease
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replay reset the paper to full size and started folding in the same
tick. The sheet's width/height transition runs .2s, so the opening and
the first fold overlapped and read as one muddled motion — which loses
the thing the replay button exists to show, namely the whole sheet
before it folds.

A 380ms pause now sits between the reset and the first crease, and the
sequence token is re-checked across it so a second replay press still
cancels cleanly. The same beat applies to the opening play, where the
paper also starts from its folded resting state.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 apps/web/public/exam-demos/SPA-PUNCH-01.html         | 8 +++++++-
 research/exam-question-types/demos/SPA-PUNCH-01.html | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

